Step 2: Prerequisites Installation 🛠️
Install these on your PC:

Node.js (v18 or higher)

Download from: https://nodejs.org/
Verify: node --version and npm --version
Python (v3.9 or higher)

Download from: https://python.org/
Verify: python --version
MongoDB (Local installation)

Download from: https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community
Or use MongoDB Atlas (cloud) for easier setup
Step 3: Backend Setup ⚙️
Navigate to backend directory:

cd backend
Create virtual environment:

python -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Mac/Linux
source venv/bin/activate
Install Python dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt
Create .env file:

# Create backend/.env file with:
MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017
Start MongoDB (if local):

Windows: Start MongoDB service
Mac: brew services start mongodb-community
Linux: sudo systemctl start mongod
Run backend server:

python server.py
Backend will run at: http://localhost:8001

Step 4: Frontend Setup 💻
Open new terminal, navigate to frontend:

cd frontend
Install dependencies:

npm install
Create .env file:

# Create frontend/.env file with:
REACT_APP_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8001
Start frontend:

npm start
Frontend will run at: http://localhost:3000

Step 5: Verify Everything Works ✅
Check backend: Visit http://localhost:8001/api/health
Check frontend: Visit http://localhost:3000
Test services: Go to http://localhost:8001/api/services
Quick Setup Script 🎯
Create this setup.sh (Mac/Linux) or setup.bat (Windows):

# Backend setup
cd backend
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
echo "MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017" > .env

# Frontend setup  
cd ../frontend
npm install
echo "REACT_APP_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8001" > .env

echo "Setup complete! Run 'python backend/server.py' and 'npm start' in frontend/"
Alternative: MongoDB Atlas (Cloud) ☁️
If you prefer cloud database:

Create MongoDB Atlas account: https://www.mongodb.com/atlas
Create cluster and get connection string
Update backend/.env:
MONGO_URL=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/carwash_db
